||| Build-time selection of the (device, dtype) pair the Idris unit
||| test suite targets. Generated from this template by the Makefile
||| rule at `Makefile`'s TESTCONFIG_IDR target — observes `PRIMARY`
||| (and the MLX_DEVICE / TORCH_DEVICE envs for hardware-variant
||| selection) and substitutes the chosen tags into this template via
||| sed. Same trick as the example-side `BuildConfig.idr` and per-build
||| `HwConfig.idr`; the test ipkg can't import either of those (they
||| live in `idris-ml-examples` / generated downstream of `Tensor`),
||| so the test sourcedir gets its own copy.
|||
||| Selection matrix (PRIMARY × hw-device env → TestDevice, TestDType):
|||
|||   tape, *                     → TapeDev,              F64
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=cpu      → TorchDev TCpu,        F64
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=mps      → TorchDev TMps,        F32
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=cuda     → TorchDev (TCuda 0),   F64
|||   mlx, MLX_DEVICE=cpu          → MlxDev MCpu,          F64
|||   mlx, MLX_DEVICE=gpu          → MlxDev MGpu,          F32
|||
||| Pre-existing unit tests (GradMode / ManagedHandle / …) used to pin
||| `{d=TapeDev}` directly; that bound them to a tape-linked dylib and
||| made `make BACKEND=torch test` / `BACKEND=mlx test` fail at FFI
||| resolution with `no entry for "tensor_create_scalar_tape"`. Tests
||| now spell `{d=TestDevice}` and resolve to the active primary at
||| build time.
|||
||| Idris-2 cannot drive type-level selection from a runtime env var —
||| types are fixed at elaboration. The generated `TestConfig.idr` is
||| in `.gitignore`. Do not edit the generated file directly; edit
||| this `.in` template instead.
module TestConfig

import public Device
import public Device.Tape
import public Device.Torch
import public Device.Mlx

||| Device tag the unit tests target. See the Selection matrix in the
||| module docstring.
public export
TestDevice : Type
TestDevice = @DEVICE@

||| DType tag the unit tests target. See the Selection matrix in the
||| module docstring.
public export
TestDType : DType
TestDType = @DTYPE@
